+## 2. Explicit Non-Goals
+
+- Do not change add-file, delete-file, move-file, permission, LSP, formatting,
+  event publication, Snapshot, or per-file atomicity behavior.
+- Do not add fuzzy replacement success. The new successful Patch branch is
+  limited to an exact literal old-block substring with a unique eligible match.
+- Do not make `apply_patch` choose one of multiple substring occurrences.
+- Do not preserve Edit whitespace-, indentation-, escape-, boundary-, or
+  anchor-normalized success after exact literal search fails. R3 removes those
+  competing replacers while preserving exact unique replacement, exact
+  multiple-match rejection, and explicit `replaceAll`.
+- Do not preserve Patch `rstrip`, `trim`, or Unicode-normalized whole-line
+  success after exact whole-line failure. The user explicitly requires the next
+  and only success mode to be exact literal substring resolution; these current
+  compatibility passes are superseded for Patch updates.
+- Do not add configuration, dependencies, migrations, generated files, or SDK
+  changes.
+- Do not use the database as a runtime dependency or add telemetry solely for
+  this repair.
+- Do not treat the current `lineIndex` as a known failure location. It is only
+  evidence for the initial lower bound; R8 replaces it with a character offset
+  cursor in the current in-memory working text that can retain position within
+  a line.
